# Source: https://bedops.github.io/docs/content/reference/file-management/conversion/vcf2bed.html
#   https://github.com/bedops/bedops/issues/258
# Symptom: chromEnd == chromStart at a non-zero position (e.g. a SNP or
#   point mutation converted from VCF with POS=12345 becoming chromStart=12344
#   chromEnd=12344 in 0-based BED).  bedops requires end > start for all
#   non-zero-length records.  Tools that represent SNPs as length-1 intervals
#   should use chromEnd = chromStart + 1.  Distinct from good/zero_length_feature.bed
#   where start==end is explicitly valid per UCSC spec for insertions;
#   this fixture tests a tool that emits equal coords by mistake (not as
#   insertion convention), causing downstream "End coordinates must be greater
#   than start coordinates" errors in bedops operations.
chr1	12344	12344	rs123456	0	+
chr1	55000	55000	rs789012	0	-
chr2	100000	100000	rs345678	0	.
